only covers finite Hilbert families; here weighted duality is used for general
inner exponents and measures. `feffermanStein_mixed` covers all exponents greater
than one and arbitrary finite inner measure spaces, with `fsMixedConst_ne_top`
certifying a constant independent of the inner space.

Reference: C. Fefferman and E. M. Stein, *Some maximal inequalities*, American
Journal of Mathematics 93 (1971), 107–115, https://doi.org/10.2307/2373450.
